    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and it passes. The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required returning `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`. I followed the codebase's established pattern for derived, read-only owner fields (like `membershipNumber`, `locality`, `identityKey`), where the value is declared in the OpenAPI schema, computed by a `@Transient` getter on the model, and auto-mapped by MapStruct.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility helper holding just the Luhn algorithm (`checkDigit(String)`, ignoring non-digits). This mirrors how `getLocality` delegates to `RegionPostcodeTable`, keeping the algorithm out of the entity and reusable.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` returning `Luhn.checkDigit(customerCode)`, or `null` before the code is assigned (consistent with `getMembershipNumber`'s null handling).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (read-only integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
